--- baseline/docs/REGRAPHICS_ADAPTIVE_FIDELITY.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ src/docs/REGRAPHICS_ADAPTIVE_FIDELITY.md	2026-11-12 07:11:29.738015949 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# REgraphics Adaptive Fidelity — new GPU Virtual capability (experimental)
+
+## Objective
+Expand fidelity of screen-space effect rendering beyond the single-pixel-cell representation without losing the original benchmark. **Path 4 remains unchanged. Path 5 is opt-in** and may be slower by design.
+
+## Actual implementation
+
+- `native/adaptive_visual_field.hpp` projects original GPU Virtual `GraphicsInstance` effects to 20-byte `VisualTile` splats.
+- Per 12-pixel cell it **only** merges nearly coincident effects with matched color, size and depth, and with a numerically bounded sampled alpha-glow deviation. Others are kept as **independent ordered splats**, not averaged into a single color or position.
+- Stable far-to-near depth order (and original input order at equal depth) preserves transparent layer ordering. RGBA is quantized to 8-bit for the GLES stream.
+- **Path 5 chooses full-resolution effects FBO** rather than the /4 FBO used in some path-4 scenes, preventing the incorrect enlargement of subpixel splats. This can raise GPU cost; it is an explicit quality tradeoff.
+- `native/visual_damage.hpp` gains `LayeredTileCache` to compare multiple RGBA/depth elements per cell, including their order; it invalidates previous/new coverage for moving or disappearing splats, handles backbuffer age and resets on context loss. Path 4 keeps its original single-tile cache.
+- `native/x_backend.cpp` preserves the same **1,024 macro anchors** on both routes 4 and 5. 369,000,000,000 is a synthetic **logical population**, not an independent-asset throughput measurement.
+- `native/scene_renderer.cpp` exposes `adaptive_field_active`, `adaptive_input`, `adaptive_tiles_merged`, `adaptive_splats_preserved`, `adaptive_risky_cells`, `adaptive_effect_divisor` in renderer capabilities. This allows objective verification of how much is actually compressed.
+- XGamingLab settings allow selecting **GPU Virtual · Fidelidad adaptativa** explicitly, alongside **GPU Virtual + REgraphics · Final**.
+
+## Ground-truth gates
+
+`bash tests/run-adaptive-fidelity.sh`:
+- Replays four previously documented destructive software cases: opaque front/back color, transparent alpha order, distinct thin objects in the same cell, small particle with correct FBO pixel size. Requires foreground MAE <= 0.008 and no accidental collapse of distinct objects.
+- Requires a genuinely safe weak-alpha same-location pair to compress and keep foreground MAE <= .006; verifies a moved point does **not** merge.
+- Tests 2 independent splats in one cache cell: unchanged frame, one moved, alpha reorder, buffer-age 2 and context reset.
+- Stress test: 100,000 independently defined sprites with distinct RGBA, positions and depth are retained as 100,000, not conflated with the 369B procedural counter. This proves data-path handling only, not physical GPU throughput.
+- Re-runs previous C01, C02, C03 and fast-route checks unchanged.
+
+`bash scripts/test-adaptive-gles.sh` (in CI with Mesa GLES2): real EGL context; compare path4 versus path5 for opaque overlap, alpha overlap and thin red/green particles with `glReadPixels`; exit nonzero on missing pixels, incorrect ordering or context errors.
+
+## Boundaries and acceptance
+
+- Not a general-purpose asset renderer and **not** proof of 369B distinct objects. Still only renders sprites/effects for `COMPACT_EFFECTS_FIELD`; exact geometry remains in the existing racing and mesh routes.
+- The risk classifier is intentionally conservative; arbitrary silhouettes, textures, and independently animated meshes must remain on exact geometry/texture paths.
+- No claim of FPS improvement or energy savings until the SM-S166V Mali-G68 measures same scene/seed/resolution, presentation FPS and internal FPS separately, P95/P99, GPU ms and screenshot parity.
+- C03 is unchanged as baseline and no PR is auto-merged. CI verifies host but cannot replace physical Mali QA.
+
+## Current validation status
+
+- Local C++ host quality and stress tests **PASS**. Source-level field tests verify four previous failure cases, safe weak-alpha compression and multi-layer dirty-region invalidation.
+- Full GLES runtime and Android/NDK build **not executed** in this container (no GLES SDK headers available). `scripts/test-adaptive-gles.sh` is prepared for an EGL/GLES CI runner.
+- 100,000 independent *splats* retained; no claim they are textured meshes or rendered frames at a specific framerate.
+- This source snapshot is an **experimental worktree**, not an upstream merged commit.
diff -ruN '--exclude=build' '--exclude=dist' '--exclude=evidence' '--exclude=signing' baseline/native/adaptive_visual_field.hpp src/native/adaptive_visual_field.hpp
--- baseline/native/adaptive_visual_field.hpp	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ src/native/adaptive_visual_field.hpp	2026-11-12 06:57:26.690242932 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+#pragma once
+// REgraphics Adaptive Fidelity: retain splats independently whenever a lossy
+// 12-pixel field merge could hide per-object color, coverage or depth.
+// This is deliberately a sprite/field capability, not an arbitrary-mesh renderer.
+#include "visual_field.hpp"
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <array>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace xlab::adaptive {
+struct Policy {
+  // A conservative error budget, expressed in physical pixels and alpha units.
+  float max_center_delta_px=.125f;
+  float max_size_delta_px=.125f;
+  float max_depth_delta=.0001f;
+  float max_rgb_delta=1.f/255.f;
+  float max_alpha_profile_error=.004f;
+  std::size_t max_merge_members=8;
+};
+struct Plan {
+  std::vector<visual::VisualTile> tiles;
+  std::size_t visible=0, projected=0, merged=0, retained=0;
+  std::size_t safe_cells=0, risky_cells=0;
+  int cell_px=12;
+};
+namespace detail {
+struct Projected {
+  visual::VisualTile tile;
+  std::array<float,4> rgba{};
+  float xpx=0,ypx=0,size=1;
+  std::size_t order=0;
+};
+inline bool mergeable(const std::vector<Projected>& src,const std::vector<std::size_t>& indices,const Policy& policy){
+  if(indices.size()<2||indices.size()>policy.max_merge_members)return false;
+  const auto& first=src[indices.front()];
+  for(const auto index:indices){
+    const auto& x=src[index];
+    if(std::abs(x.xpx-first.xpx)>policy.max_center_delta_px||
+       std::abs(x.ypx-first.ypx)>policy.max_center_delta_px||
+       std::abs(x.size-first.size)>policy.max_size_delta_px||
+       std::abs(x.tile.depth-first.tile.depth)>policy.max_depth_delta)return false;
+    for(int k=0;k<3;++k)if(std::abs(x.rgba[k]-first.rgba[k])>policy.max_rgb_delta)return false;
+  }
+  // A single alpha at the center cannot in general reproduce repeated
+  // alpha*glow blends away from the center. Check their profile directly.
+  double center_transmission=1.0;
+  for(auto index:indices)center_transmission*=1.0-src[index].rgba[3];
+  const double merged_alpha=1.0-center_transmission;
+  for(int i=0;i<=16;++i){
+    const double glow=double(i)/16.;
+    double transmission=1.0;
+    for(auto index:indices)transmission*=1.0-double(src[index].rgba[3])*glow;
+    if(std::abs((1.0-transmission)-merged_alpha*glow)>policy.max_alpha_profile_error)return false;
+  }
+  return true;
+}
+} // namespace detail
+
+inline Plan build(const std::vector<const xgpu::GraphicsInstance*>& visible,
+                  const visual::M4& view_projection,int width,int height,int cell_px=12,
+                  const Policy& policy={}){
+  Plan out;out.visible=visible.size();out.cell_px=std::max(4,cell_px);
+  if(width<=0||height<=0||visible.empty())return out;
+  const int cols=(width+out.cell_px-1)/out.cell_px,rows=(height+out.cell_px-1)/out.cell_px;
+  std::vector<detail::Projected> projections;projections.reserve(visible.size());
+  std::vector<int> heads(std::size_t(cols)*rows,-1),previous;previous.reserve(visible.size());
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<visible.size();++i){
+    const auto* item=visible[i];if(!item)continue;
+    const auto c=visual::clip(view_projection,*item);
+    if(!(c[3]>1.e-5f)||!std::isfinite(c[3]))continue;
+    const float nx=c[0]/c[3],ny=c[1]/c[3],ndc_depth=c[2]/c[3];
+    if(!std::isfinite(nx)||!std::isfinite(ny)||!std::isfinite(ndc_depth)||
+       nx<-1.1f||nx>1.1f||ny<-1.1f||ny>1.1f)continue;
+    const auto& q=item->payload;
+    if(!std::isfinite(q[3])||!std::isfinite(q[7]))continue;
+    bool invalid=false;for(int k=12;k<16;++k)invalid|=!std::isfinite(q[k]);
+    if(invalid)continue;
+    detail::Projected x;
+    x.xpx=(nx*.5f+.5f)*width;x.ypx=(ny*.5f+.5f)*height;
+    x.size=std::clamp(std::abs(view_projection[5])*std::max(q[3],q[7])*height/
+                        std::max(std::abs(c[3]),.02f),1.f,96.f);
+    x.tile.ndc_x=nx;x.tile.ndc_y=ny;
+    x.tile.depth=std::clamp(ndc_depth*.5f+.5f,0.f,1.f);
+    x.tile.size_px=x.size;x.order=i;
+    for(int k=0;k<4;++k){x.rgba[k]=std::clamp(q[12+k],0.f,1.f);x.tile.color[std::size_t(k)]=visual::byte(x.rgba[k]);}
+    const int cx=std::clamp(int(x.xpx/out.cell_px),0,cols-1),cy=std::clamp(int(x.ypx/out.cell_px),0,rows-1);
+    const auto cell=std::size_t(cy)*cols+cx;
+    previous.push_back(heads[cell]);heads[cell]=int(projections.size());
+    projections.push_back(x);++out.projected;
+  }
+  struct Ordered {visual::VisualTile tile;std::size_t index;};
+  std::vector<Ordered> sorted;sorted.reserve(projections.size());
+  std::vector<std::size_t> indices;indices.reserve(16);
+  for(const int head:heads){
+    if(head<0)continue;
+    indices.clear();
+    for(int cursor=head;cursor>=0;cursor=previous[std::size_t(cursor)])indices.push_back(std::size_t(cursor));
+    std::reverse(indices.begin(),indices.end());
+    if(!detail::mergeable(projections,indices,policy)){
+      if(indices.size()>1)++out.risky_cells;
+      out.retained+=indices.size();
+      for(const auto index:indices)sorted.push_back({projections[index].tile,projections[index].order});
+      continue;
+    }
+    // Very nearly identical weak-alpha splats: only this case is compressed.
+    ++out.safe_cells;out.merged+=indices.size()-1;
+    double transmission=1.;
+    for(auto index:indices)transmission*=1.0-projections[index].rgba[3];
+    auto result=projections[indices.front()].tile;
+    result.color[3]=visual::byte(float(1.0-transmission));
+    sorted.push_back({result,projections[indices.front()].order});
+  }
+  std::stable_sort(sorted.begin(),sorted.end(),[](const Ordered&a,const Ordered&b){
+    if(a.tile.depth!=b.tile.depth)return a.tile.depth>b.tile.depth;
+    return a.index<b.index;
+  });
+  for(const auto& item:sorted)out.tiles.push_back(item.tile);
+  return out;
+}
+} // namespace xlab::adaptive
